class.description:
A [VideoPreset] bundles the settings that [method VideoPresetSettingsServer.apply_preset] sets in the settings domains [code]"render_quality"[/code] ([RenderQualitySettingsServer]), [code]"texture"[/code] ([TextureSettingsServer]), [code]"shadow"[/code] ([ShadowSettingsServer]) and [code]"render_effect"[/code] ([RenderEffectSettingsServer]). Each domain has a typed resource of the class the domain stores ([RenderQualitySettings], [TextureSettings], [ShadowSettings], [RenderEffectSettings]), so the Inspector shows its enums and ranges. A domain resource sets [i]all[/i] values of its domain; a [code]null[/code] resource leaves the domain as it is, so a preset can cover only some domains.
The four built-in presets are created with [method VideoPresetSettingsServer.create_builtin_preset]. To replace or add presets, save a [VideoPreset] as a [code].tres[/code] file and add it to [member ProjectSettings.settings/video_preset/presets], or call [method VideoPresetSettingsServer.add_preset] at runtime. The window settings ([WindowSettingsServer]) are not part of a preset.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var preset = VideoPresetSettingsServer.create_builtin_preset("High")
preset.preset_name = "Cinematic"
preset.render_effect.dof_blur_quality = RenderingServer.DOF_BLUR_QUALITY_HIGH
preset.render_quality.scaling_3d_scale = 1.5
VideoPresetSettingsServer.add_preset(preset)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
VideoPreset preset = VideoPresetSettingsServer.CreateBuiltinPreset("High");
preset.PresetName = "Cinematic";
preset.RenderEffect.DofBlurQuality = RenderingServer.DofBlurQuality.High;
preset.RenderQuality.Scaling3DScale = 1.5f;
VideoPresetSettingsServer.AddPreset(preset);
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] Use values a domain accepts unchanged (for example powers of two for shadow atlas sizes). A value the domain clamps or rounds no longer matches the preset after it is applied, so the next change of any value of the preset shows [code]"Custom"[/code].
